WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:03.890
Colonel Rhodes.

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:05.270
Glad to see you could make it, son.

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:07.010
I feel safer already.

00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:10.260
Evy Poumpouras: I will take a
Secret Service agent any day

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:12.960
over anything like that.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:15.140
Hi, everyone. My name is Evy Poumpouras.

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:18.840
I'm a former special agent
with the US Secret Service,

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.500
and I was also on the
Presidential Protective Division

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:25.260
for Barack Obama and
first lady Michelle Obama.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:28.610
I've also protected
presidents George H. W. Bush,

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:31.400
George Bush, and Bill Clinton.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.680
Today, I'm going to be
watching movie and TV clips

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:37.770
and letting you know how real or not real

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:39.128
I think that they are.

00:00:42.501 --> 00:00:45.076
[audience applauding]

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:51.040
The first thing I noticed with this clip

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:54.380
is the president of the
United States is in the crowd

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:55.830
shaking hands with people.

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:57.380
That would really not happen.

00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:01.280
In real life when we're doing protection,

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:03.850
you won't see the
president go into the crowd

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:05.640
or into the table area.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:07.690
Typically, a rope line is created

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:10.010
within some distance from the stage,

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:11.340
usually several feet,

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:14.220
and people will line up by that rope line,

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:16.010
and the president will go then

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:17.690
and shake those people's hands.

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:19.450
So there's always a barrier.

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:21.493
There's always something separating

00:01:21.493 --> 00:01:23.630
the president from the people.

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:25.680
He, or she, maybe, in the future,

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:28.258
but he will not be in that crowd.

00:01:28.258 --> 00:01:30.810
[ominous music]

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:32.152
[gunshot]

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:36.050
That's not make believe.

00:01:36.050 --> 00:01:37.720
That is very, very real.

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:39.900
That is your job as a
Secret Service agent.

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:41.110
Your job is to take a bullet.

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:43.440
Not only just to jump
in front of the bullet,

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:46.195
but to get into the way

00:01:46.195 --> 00:01:48.330
and to make yourself as big as possible.

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:51.050
So, you're also taught to expand your body

00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:54.020
to make sure that the
bullet actually hits you

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:55.865
and doesn't miss you and hit

00:01:55.865 --> 00:01:57.450
the president of the United States.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.150
Through all the tactical
training that you go through

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:02.090
in the Secret Service Academy,

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:03.515
this is a movement that you do

00:02:03.515 --> 00:02:05.665
over and over and over again.

00:02:05.665 --> 00:02:07.780
It's also a Secret Service mindset.

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:10.130
When you go through training
and if you enter this job,

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:12.440
like, you are at that point

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:15.789
comfortable and fully OK with
doing something like this.

00:02:15.789 --> 00:02:18.239
[dramatic music]

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:22.440
The shift's job is to
assess the environment.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:23.390
They're always looking out.

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:26.550
And the potential threat
is someone who can do harm.

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:28.621
The No. 1 thing to look for, honestly,

00:02:28.621 --> 00:02:30.300
is the hands. You wanna see hands,

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.900
and I always would wanna
see hands, open hands.

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:34.240
So if the hands are out and open,

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:37.150
then I know that there's
nothing in those hands.

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:38.790
On occasion, you might get somebody

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:40.970
who unintentionally is
maybe holding something,

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:42.710
holding even a pen.

00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:44.520
And when you see that, I mean, literally,

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.920
we just knock that pen out of their hands.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:49.060
If somebody has their
hands in their pockets

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:50.460
and they're unwilling to take them out,

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:53.240
or if there's not enough
time to get those hands out,

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:56.310
I mean, you literally would
just grab that person's hands,

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:59.870
lock them down until the president passes.

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:02.803
Based on realism on one to 10,

00:03:02.803 --> 00:03:04.903
I would actually give this,

00:03:04.903 --> 00:03:07.079
I would give this a seven.

00:03:07.079 --> 00:03:09.950
[dramatic music]

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:12.633
Mike: Mr. Secretary, get
away from the window, now.

00:03:12.633 --> 00:03:14.410
We need to leave, now.

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:16.740
Evy: We see the detail leader

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:19.890
go over to where Kiefer
Sutherland is standing,

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:22.360
and he actually closes the windows,

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:24.110
and he tells him, "Sir,
get away from the window."

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:25.180
That is absolutely correct.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:27.460
That is absolutely what
I would do as well.

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:30.000
You would want to get them
out of the area of danger,

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.320
and you'd want to put
them in an environment

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:34.168
where they are safe, some type of bunker.

00:03:34.168 --> 00:03:35.463
Alex: Tom!
Tom: Did you see that?

00:03:35.463 --> 00:03:36.630
Alex: Tom!
Tom: Did you see that?

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:37.870
Mike: Smoke out any ambush.

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:39.860
White House is secure. Let's go.

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:41.635
Evy: I would not take

00:03:41.635 --> 00:03:44.285
the future president of the United States

00:03:44.285 --> 00:03:46.010
back to the White House.

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:47.060
Absolutely not.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:49.410
The swearing-in ceremony
can wait till later.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.030
You'd wanna take the president

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:54.360
to an undisclosed safe location,

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:57.270
keep him there for some time
until things have settled,

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:59.210
and then you can figure
out what to do next.

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:01.140
So, on 9/11, what did they
do with the president?

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:02.447
They grabbed the president,

00:04:02.447 --> 00:04:04.505
and they actually kept
him on Air Force One,

00:04:04.505 --> 00:04:06.530
and they flew around.

00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:07.995
Mike: It's confirmed.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:10.330
Eagle is gone.

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:11.930
Evy: In this scene, we see the president

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:14.560
being referred to as Eagle, his code name.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:16.550
Every administration gets code names.

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:18.680
And, typically, the code names

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:20.290
all begin with the same letter.

00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:22.640
So, for the Clintons, it was an E.

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:24.613
Everybody in the Clinton administration,

00:04:24.613 --> 00:04:26.960
or the protectees, they all had E's.

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:30.230
For president George W. Bush, it was a T.

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:32.260
And so, essentially,
all the family members,

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:35.000
first lady, president, the children,

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.860
they all had code names
beginning with a T.

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:40.640
So they do change for
every administration.

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:43.760
And the code name actually
stays with the person

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:46.697
even after they leave the presidency.

00:04:46.697 --> 00:04:49.833
[ominous music]

00:04:49.833 --> 00:04:50.866
Man: Gun!

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:55.220
Evy: Where are my snipers?

00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:57.340
Snipers are there to actually look

00:04:57.340 --> 00:04:58.880
for the threat that's coming from above.

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:00.710
Here we see an open window.

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:03.740
The snipers are tactically placed

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:05.190
throughout the environment,

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:06.980
and they're put in elevated positions

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:09.280
so they can see elevated threats.

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:12.640
So they're actually working in
tandem with the ground team,

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:13.930
and they call out the positions.

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:15.260
They call out the threats.

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:16.850
The ground team is what responds.

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:17.740
They are active.

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:19.100
They are seeing, "Open window!"

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:20.590
They are seeing somebody moving.

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:22.220
They are seeing somebody at a rooftop,

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:24.330
and immediately somebody is responding.

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:26.062
Your sniper team up top is the one

00:05:26.062 --> 00:05:27.240
who's gonna see the threat.

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:28.360
They're gonna engage the threat,

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:31.290
and they're gonna take that threat out.

00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:33.160
On a scale of one to 10,

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:34.885
I would give this one a three.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:37.940
Mike: Get down!
[gunfire]

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:42.550
Evy: I have a really
hard time with this clip,

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:45.480
because there's so many things
in here that are not true,

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:48.870
which makes kind of the
whole thing not real.

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:50.440
The cars, the cars, the cars.

00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:52.630
The Beast. There's only one Beast in this.

00:05:52.630 --> 00:05:54.435
There's always gonna be two Beasts.

00:05:54.435 --> 00:05:56.530
And not only are you gonna
have two ballistic limos,

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:58.990
you're also gonna have
multiple follow-up vehicles,

00:05:58.990 --> 00:06:00.550
which tend to be Suburban,

00:06:00.550 --> 00:06:02.730
which are also ballistic.

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:03.820
Your emergency vehicle,

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:05.810
which is showing up to save the day,

00:06:05.810 --> 00:06:07.100
that's going to be there.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:08.790
You're not gonna have
this emergency vehicle

00:06:08.790 --> 00:06:10.450
showing up from nowhere.

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:13.870
Now, here, we also see this
internal ambush happening.

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:17.800
In the inner circle of the president,

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:21.640
although we have help,
you have police help,

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:23.860
they typically tend to
be at the outskirts.

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:26.000
In the inner circle of protection,

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:28.018
it's always gonna be US Secret Service.

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:31.240
[gunfire]

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:32.490
Mike: All right, back to the car!

00:06:33.980 --> 00:06:36.380
Evy: So, here's why there's
a technical error here.

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:37.570
The building, we see the building,

00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:39.210
somebody closes the doors.

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:40.120
That would never happen.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:41.530
There's always an agent there,

00:06:41.530 --> 00:06:44.060
and that agent's job is to make sure

00:06:44.060 --> 00:06:45.380
that those doors are open

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:48.900
so that the president can
run back in if he needs to.

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:50.540
The other thing is, the vehicle door,

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:52.640
that vehicle door will also stay open.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:54.580
So, basically, what you're ensuring

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:57.540
is the president can either go
into the car if he needs to,

00:06:57.540 --> 00:06:59.980
into the Beast, or back into the building.

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:01.620
And here we see them stuck outside,

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:04.678
which should absolutely never happen.

00:07:06.044 --> 00:07:07.460
Mike: Move it! Down!

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:12.630
Evy: That is a ballistic vehicle.

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:16.280
The Beast is called the
Beast for a specific reason.

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:19.720
The Beast is designed to take
a beating and keep going.

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:22.240
When you travel to another country,

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:24.990
you make sure to do advance work.

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:27.781
Advance work means sending agents

00:07:27.781 --> 00:07:31.397
out there in advance for
weeks at a time sometimes,

00:07:31.397 --> 00:07:33.787
maybe even a month, to
prepare for a visit.

00:07:33.787 --> 00:07:35.780
That means you work very closely

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:37.260
with the local police department,

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:38.930
the local law-enforcement entities,

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:41.410
the local intelligence entities.

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:43.590
It is the proactive element.

00:07:43.590 --> 00:07:45.430
It's everything you've done beforehand.

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:47.530
So when I see this
image, I have a problem.

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:49.170
Where are my snipers?

00:07:49.170 --> 00:07:50.700
Should be snipers there.

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:51.970
Where's the tactical team?

00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:53.760
There should be a tactical team there.

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:54.880
Where are the long weapons?

00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:57.280
Secret Service shift agents
also have long weapons.

00:07:57.280 --> 00:07:58.880
Where are those?

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:02.125
I wanna give it a zero, but let's give it,

00:08:02.125 --> 00:08:03.477
I would give it a two.

00:08:05.945 --> 00:08:07.254
Doug: This way, ma'am.

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:14.720
Evy: Nicolas Cage is
actually trying to get Tess

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:16.760
to get in through his door,

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:18.730
the passenger-side door.

00:08:18.730 --> 00:08:20.460
What he's doing is correct.

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:22.000
Typically, you will see the protectee

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:23.810
going in through that specific door,

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:25.780
the door behind the passenger.

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:27.500
And we see the detail leader,

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:29.620
which is Nicolas Cage in this part,

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:31.400
sitting in the front seat.

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:34.990
The door that's closest to her front door

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:38.390
is the passenger-side door of the vehicle.

00:08:38.390 --> 00:08:41.240
A protectee needs to go in
through the closest door.

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:43.300
So what's the closest
door to my front door?

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:44.930
The passenger-side door.

00:08:44.930 --> 00:08:46.890
The issue here is you
don't want the protectee

00:08:46.890 --> 00:08:48.420
coming out the front door,

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:51.660
then walking around the
vehicle to the other side.

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:53.703
That's the issue there.

00:08:53.703 --> 00:08:54.650
Doug: Ma'am, excuse me,

00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:55.970
but we are not leaving this house

00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:57.220
until you are seated properly

00:08:57.220 --> 00:09:00.260
with your seat belt firmly fastened.

00:09:00.260 --> 00:09:01.670
Evy: You have to lay the law down,

00:09:01.670 --> 00:09:05.254
and I probably would have
done what Nicolas Cage did.

00:09:05.254 --> 00:09:08.504
[dramatic opera music]
[Tess snoring]

00:09:13.487 --> 00:09:14.320
[Tess screams]

00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:19.010
Your duty is to physically protect them,

00:09:19.010 --> 00:09:21.810
but you're also there to
shield them from many things.

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:23.530
I definitely would not do what he did,

00:09:23.530 --> 00:09:25.288
kind of shaking her up like that,

00:09:25.288 --> 00:09:26.790
but I would nudge her.

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:29.036
I would maybe draw the curtains

00:09:29.036 --> 00:09:31.010
down at the side and shield her.

00:09:31.010 --> 00:09:33.631
I would give it an eight.

00:09:35.127 --> 00:09:36.110
[sirens wailing]

00:09:36.110 --> 00:09:37.282
Pete: Get me a perimeter!

00:09:37.282 --> 00:09:40.399
10 meters! 360 degrees!

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:44.990
Evy: Yeah, there's a lot
of issues with this one.

00:09:44.990 --> 00:09:47.660
One is, how on earth did he end up

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:49.450
in the middle there with his protectee?

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:52.660
That's, I wanna say impossible,

00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:55.960
but that's highly,
highly, highly unlikely.

00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:58.960
Why is there so much distance
between the vehicles and them?

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:01.115
The vehicles should actually pull up

00:10:01.115 --> 00:10:03.350
super close to them to shield them.

00:10:03.350 --> 00:10:06.041
My other thing is, we see the first lady

00:10:06.041 --> 00:10:07.216
in this movie jump out,

00:10:07.216 --> 00:10:09.030
which is played by Kim Basinger.

00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:11.360
She jumps out, and she's the middle of it.

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:13.360
Where's her detail leader?

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:15.320
Each protectee has a detail leader,

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:17.100
meaning the president has their own person

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:19.790
who protects them, and their shift,

00:10:19.790 --> 00:10:23.270
and then the first lady has her
own person who protects her,

00:10:23.270 --> 00:10:26.070
her detail leader and her shift.

00:10:26.070 --> 00:10:29.480
So there's two protection
elements, not one.

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:33.280
So, we do see Michael
Douglas call out formations

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:37.090
or degrees or angles as to
where he wants people to go.

00:10:37.090 --> 00:10:38.880
That's not something that we do.

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:42.920
There are formations, and
these are prechoreographed,

00:10:42.920 --> 00:10:44.950
predesigned formations that we use.

00:10:44.950 --> 00:10:47.060
And we know when and how to use them.

00:10:47.060 --> 00:10:49.662
And the detail leader can, on occasion,

00:10:49.662 --> 00:10:51.150
sporadically call them out.

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:52.850
But when we are being attacked,

00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:55.230
everybody automatically knows where to go

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:57.210
and everybody has their own position,

00:10:57.210 --> 00:10:59.750
depending on the type of attack.

00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:02.913
On a scale of one to 10,
I would give it a three.

00:11:05.770 --> 00:11:07.330
Ellis: Colonel Rhodes.

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:08.850
Glad to see you can make it, son.

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:10.500
I feel safer already.

00:11:13.930 --> 00:11:16.240
Evy: One, why isn't he ID'd?

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:17.970
I mean, make him lift up his mask.

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:18.960
I don't know who he is.

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:23.010
He's in this costume and
you can't see him, No. 1.

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:26.690
No. 2, nobody, as far as I'm concerned,

00:11:26.690 --> 00:11:29.790
gets on that plane with guns

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:31.590
other than US Secret Service agents.

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:34.350
You can sense sometimes
that there's a problem

00:11:34.350 --> 00:11:36.410
without even being able to articulate

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:37.540
that there's a problem.

00:11:37.540 --> 00:11:40.790
I will take a Secret Service agent any day

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:43.040
over anything like that.

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:44.743
Air Force One is actually

00:11:44.743 --> 00:11:47.690
the responsibility of the Air Force.

00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:50.220
The Air Force protects the
plane, they maintain the plane,

00:11:50.220 --> 00:11:52.290
and when the president isn't on the plane,

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:54.600
they actually do security for it.

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:57.660
Members of the Air Force
are allowed on the plane,

00:11:57.660 --> 00:11:59.690
members of the staff are
allowed on the plane,

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:02.130
and Secret Service agents
are allowed on the plane.

00:12:02.130 --> 00:12:03.740
I have access to my weapons.

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:05.357
We have access to all our weapons.

00:12:05.357 --> 00:12:07.670
I mean, we need our weapons on the plane.

00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:09.630
And we have other weapons

00:12:09.630 --> 00:12:11.810
aside from the ones
that we personally carry

00:12:11.810 --> 00:12:14.103
that we haul on and off the plane.

00:12:14.985 --> 00:12:17.818
[gunfire]

00:12:20.210 --> 00:12:24.000
Yes, you can use your weapon on the plane.

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:26.950
However, you have to be very, very careful

00:12:26.950 --> 00:12:28.250
when you do use that weapon.

00:12:28.250 --> 00:12:30.310
You have to be super
careful, super accurate,

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:31.650
because if you miss,

00:12:31.650 --> 00:12:34.050
you could blow a hole into the side

00:12:34.050 --> 00:12:35.670
or a portion of the plane,

00:12:35.670 --> 00:12:37.680
which could then cause a serious problem

00:12:37.680 --> 00:12:39.560
to the aircraft itself.

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:40.700
I'll give it a one.

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:44.050
I only give it a one for just
certain technical aspects

00:12:44.050 --> 00:12:46.340
as far as, like, the way
the limo's pulling up,

00:12:46.340 --> 00:12:48.505
the way the plane is positioned.

00:12:48.505 --> 00:12:51.350
[ominous music]

00:12:51.350 --> 00:12:52.183
Sawyer: Gentlemen.

00:12:53.243 --> 00:12:55.211
What are you doing?

00:12:55.211 --> 00:12:56.044
Martin!

00:12:56.044 --> 00:12:58.060
Walker: Consider this my resignation.

00:12:58.060 --> 00:13:01.053
Evy: So, how suspicious should
you be of your colleagues?

00:13:01.890 --> 00:13:04.580
I was in the US Secret
Service for over 12 years.

00:13:04.580 --> 00:13:06.770
I was never suspicious of my colleagues,

00:13:06.770 --> 00:13:08.200
not in this level.

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:09.675
To be a double agent,

00:13:09.675 --> 00:13:13.550
to get into the US Secret
Service as a double agent,

00:13:13.550 --> 00:13:15.660
that is not an easy thing to do.

00:13:15.660 --> 00:13:17.740
So, here's the thing.
There's a hiring process.

00:13:17.740 --> 00:13:21.830
A very, very involved hiring process.

00:13:21.830 --> 00:13:24.900
A hiring process with
multiple layers of protection,

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:29.290
of security, so that somebody
like that cannot get in.

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:31.350
They do such a deep dive

00:13:31.350 --> 00:13:34.660
and intensive background
investigation on you.

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:35.950
You're talking background checks,

00:13:35.950 --> 00:13:38.220
you're talking about
interviewing people's families,

00:13:38.220 --> 00:13:39.990
their schools, going
through their history,

00:13:39.990 --> 00:13:44.240
their previous jobs, their
employers, polygraph tests.

00:13:44.240 --> 00:13:46.640
I used to give polygraphs
and assess people

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:48.930
on the veracity of the truthfulness

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:51.220
of what they were saying
in their application.

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:53.274
To have an agent pull their gun out

00:13:53.274 --> 00:13:56.073
and shoot one of their
brothers and sisters?

00:13:57.700 --> 00:14:00.130
I can't see that. I really can't.

00:14:00.130 --> 00:14:01.930
I have a bit of a hard
time with this scene

00:14:01.930 --> 00:14:04.140
because we see Jamie Foxx, the president,

00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:05.910
going down into this bunker.

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:08.480
No. 1, let me just say, Jamie Foxx,

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:10.610
the president, is not
the one clearing the way

00:14:10.610 --> 00:14:12.250
and getting access to the bunker.

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:14.700
His team, his Secret Service agents,

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:16.460
if there were to be a bunker,

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:17.920
they're the ones clearing the way

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:19.310
making sure he can get in.

00:14:19.310 --> 00:14:21.140
We're talking about the White House.

00:14:21.140 --> 00:14:24.900
We're talking about a lot
of Secret Service agents.

00:14:24.900 --> 00:14:27.620
Not just agents, but uniform division.

00:14:27.620 --> 00:14:29.250
It is highly unlikely.

00:14:29.250 --> 00:14:32.420
Again, I never wanna say
never, but if not impossible,

00:14:32.420 --> 00:14:34.110
where the whole team is taken out,

00:14:34.110 --> 00:14:36.150
and you have Channing Tatum,

00:14:36.150 --> 00:14:37.331
some member of the public,

00:14:37.331 --> 00:14:39.006
show up to end up protecting

00:14:39.006 --> 00:14:41.380
the president of the United States,

00:14:42.790 --> 00:14:44.170
probably impossible.

00:14:44.170 --> 00:14:48.560
As far as your protectee being
able to protect themselves,

00:14:48.560 --> 00:14:51.460
their job is not to take self-defense.

00:14:51.460 --> 00:14:54.160
Their job is not to learn self-defense.

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:56.340
And so that's why the
Secret Service is there.

00:14:56.340 --> 00:14:58.040
You're not there to
teach them self-defense.

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:01.290
You're there to do the
self-defense for them.

00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:04.363
I would give it a zero.

00:15:06.006 --> 00:15:07.164
Agent: Mr. President.
Bartlet: What the hell?

00:15:07.164 --> 00:15:08.560
Agent: Step away from the window, please.

00:15:08.560 --> 00:15:11.020
Bartlet: OK, you know what, I'm
gonna have to call you back.

00:15:11.020 --> 00:15:12.270
Ron: Three shots were
fired from the street,

00:15:12.270 --> 00:15:14.890
at least one of them hitting
the press briefing room.

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:16.360
We've got the suspect in custody

00:15:16.360 --> 00:15:17.650
as well as a high-powered rifle.

00:15:17.650 --> 00:15:18.740
Bartlet: Was anyone in the room?

00:15:18.740 --> 00:15:22.770
Evy: If there is any type of
shooting at the White House,

00:15:22.770 --> 00:15:25.030
the last place I would want to go to

00:15:25.030 --> 00:15:26.940
to have a nice discussion
with the president

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:29.810
about the shooting is in the Oval Office.

00:15:29.810 --> 00:15:31.550
Oval Office is glass.

00:15:31.550 --> 00:15:34.400
There's doors. There's windows.
It's open. It's exposed.

00:15:34.400 --> 00:15:36.270
Although it is protected,

00:15:36.270 --> 00:15:40.290
it is commonly known that it
is not a truly secure area.

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:42.290
When the president is at the Oval Office,

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:44.940
there are always Secret Service agents.

00:15:44.940 --> 00:15:47.720
They are outside, and they are inside.

00:15:47.720 --> 00:15:51.160
I would give this a one
on a scale of one to 10,

00:15:51.160 --> 00:15:52.280
just simply for the fact

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:55.650
that you truly would
never have a conversation

00:15:55.650 --> 00:15:57.430
with your protectee like that,

00:15:57.430 --> 00:16:00.863
when shots were just fired
in such close proximity.

00:16:02.292 --> 00:16:03.533
Simms: I'm back, I'm back.

00:16:03.533 --> 00:16:05.100
Woods: Back off, Simms!

00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:06.700
I don't got a problem with you.

00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:07.883
Simms: You hurt this kid,

00:16:07.883 --> 00:16:09.332
you're gonna have problems
with me. All right?

00:16:09.332 --> 00:16:10.580
You're gonna have problems with everybody.

00:16:10.580 --> 00:16:11.787
So why don't you just let the kid go?

00:16:11.787 --> 00:16:12.620
Woods: Shut up!

00:16:12.620 --> 00:16:16.070
Evy: I've actually protected
children of a president,

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:18.540
a specific child I was assigned to.

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:21.480
Now, my first question is,
where's everybody else?

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:22.880
Where's the team?

00:16:22.880 --> 00:16:25.770
You're never alone with
just the protectee.

00:16:25.770 --> 00:16:28.180
Even if it's a child, you have a team.

00:16:28.180 --> 00:16:30.740
I really would be
mindful as to who I allow

00:16:30.740 --> 00:16:33.580
in close proximity of my protectee.

00:16:33.580 --> 00:16:35.610
Usually, people that they know very well

00:16:35.610 --> 00:16:37.740
are allowed access to them.

00:16:37.740 --> 00:16:41.518
People that are vetted are
allowed access to them.

00:16:41.518 --> 00:16:42.910
Simms: Now, look, calm down.

00:16:42.910 --> 00:16:44.616
The mall full of people,
man. They're shopping, huh?

00:16:44.616 --> 00:16:45.780
Got women, got children.

00:16:45.780 --> 00:16:47.690
You don't wanna shoot anybody.

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:50.670
Evy: I might spend time
distracting the person,

00:16:50.670 --> 00:16:53.160
but I'm not gonna sit
and negotiate with you.

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:54.690
I'll distract you and talk to you

00:16:54.690 --> 00:16:58.260
so that my teams can come in
from behind and take you out,

00:16:58.260 --> 00:17:01.730
so that I can regain
control of my protectee

00:17:01.730 --> 00:17:04.120
and keep my protectee safe.

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:05.570
I might give this one a five.

00:17:07.199 --> 00:17:08.989
[upbeat music]

00:17:08.989 --> 00:17:11.322
[clamoring]

00:17:12.290 --> 00:17:16.060
So, we have Kevin Costner
protecting a celebrity.

00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:17.600
This isn't uncommon, actually.

00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:21.760
A lot of Secret Service
agents, when they retire,

00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:23.430
they typically end up going into

00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:25.200
some form of private security.

00:17:25.200 --> 00:17:26.485
He's on stage,

00:17:26.485 --> 00:17:28.510
but I'm trying to figure
out exactly where he is,

00:17:28.510 --> 00:17:29.917
but typically he's supposed to be

00:17:29.917 --> 00:17:31.920
on stage, but in the back.

00:17:31.920 --> 00:17:34.500
Either stage right or stage left.

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:37.740
The other issue is you have
people on stage with her.

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:40.030
Definitely a huge, huge no-no.

00:17:40.030 --> 00:17:41.730
There's nobody that's gonna be on stage,

00:17:41.730 --> 00:17:44.190
because, as we see, she gets ambushed.

00:17:44.190 --> 00:17:47.460
Again, you wanna make sure
that when you're an agent,

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:49.860
there is nothing, and I mean nothing,

00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:52.223
between you and your protectee.

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:54.836
Frank: Tony!
Tony: I'll take care of this!

00:17:54.836 --> 00:17:56.202
Frank: Not there!

00:17:56.202 --> 00:17:57.990
Tony: Follow me!

00:17:57.990 --> 00:17:59.830
Evy: Interestingly enough, where you see

00:17:59.830 --> 00:18:03.590
the other security person
tell, wave him to come to him,

00:18:03.590 --> 00:18:06.240
your evacuation point should
not be through the crowd.

00:18:06.240 --> 00:18:08.050
It should not be through
where the front doors are.

00:18:08.050 --> 00:18:10.930
I want an exit that is away from everyone.

00:18:10.930 --> 00:18:13.080
I want an exit that nobody uses.

00:18:13.080 --> 00:18:15.530
The proper thing to do is,

00:18:15.530 --> 00:18:17.830
she's behind you, and
so long as she can move.

00:18:17.830 --> 00:18:18.790
She's behind you.

00:18:18.790 --> 00:18:20.920
You're creating the shield,
and you're using your hands

00:18:20.920 --> 00:18:23.590
and you're pushing people away,
and then you're going out.

00:18:23.590 --> 00:18:25.790
You really don't want her
or anything in your hands.

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:28.030
That's why, even if you see

00:18:28.030 --> 00:18:29.913
bad weather outside and it's raining,

00:18:29.913 --> 00:18:32.750
you'll never see an agent
holding an umbrella.

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:35.130
You'll never see an
agent even holding bags

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:35.990
or anything in their hands.

00:18:35.990 --> 00:18:38.170
Hands are the most important thing.

00:18:38.170 --> 00:18:39.190
These are your weapons.

00:18:39.190 --> 00:18:40.837
This is your defense system.

00:18:40.837 --> 00:18:42.690
And if there's something in your hands,

00:18:42.690 --> 00:18:45.110
how can you actually
fight and protect someone?

00:18:45.110 --> 00:18:49.140
This not being a true
Secret Service protectee,

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:52.490
I mean, I can see how this
can happen in real life.

00:18:52.490 --> 00:18:55.633
I would give this a six.

00:18:56.470 --> 00:18:58.090
You'd wanna take the president

00:18:58.090 --> 00:19:01.430
to an undisclosed, safe location,

00:19:01.430 --> 00:19:04.340
keep him there for some time
until things have settled,

00:19:04.340 --> 00:19:06.515
and then you can figure
out what to do next.

